 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Therapy Intake Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a counseling intake form?\", \"a\": \"A counseling intake form is the questionnaire a new client completes before the first session. The name is used interchangeably with therapy intake form. It asks for contact details, the reason for seeking help, past treatment, and signed consent. The counselor starts the first hour already knowing the basics.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a therapy intake form?\", \"a\": \"List what a new client should answer before the session, and mark the answers someone has to see first. Describe that list to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, which builds the form and the database behind it. Put screener scoring and private links for partners in the same prompt. Any later change is another prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a therapy intake form include?\", \"a\": \"Most cover five areas: contact details, the reason the client is seeking help now, past treatment and medications, family background, and any screening questionnaires. Consent pages and a signature close the form. Keep to facts a client can give without help; the story behind the concern is for the session.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free therapy intake form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Many practices post their intake packets online, and free printable counseling intake forms are easy to find. A printed copy still has to be typed up and scored by hand. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing the form at a live URL, with each response stored as a record.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions are on a behavioral health intake form?\", \"a\": \"The core therapy intake questions, plus substance use, psychiatric history, and any current prescriber. If your clinic bills insurance, add the plan details and a release to coordinate care with the client's primary care doctor. A medical office asks mostly about physical health instead, on a patient intake form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do clinics use a mental health intake form?\", \"a\": \"Mostly to plan the first appointment. Staff read it to decide which clinician fits and how soon the client should be seen. Screener totals and any answer about self-harm go to a clinician before anything else. The rest becomes the starting point for the assessment and the intake note.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which screening questions belong on an intake form for mental health?\", \"a\": \"Start with the PHQ-9 for depression and the GAD-7 for anxiety, nine and seven questions long. PHQ-9 totals run 0 to 27 and GAD-7 totals 0 to 21, and a score of 10 marks the moderate band on both. Item 9 of the PHQ-9 asks about self-harm. Anything but Not at all there needs follow-up by someone trained to assess suicide risk.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I use one counseling intake form template for couples and teens?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if its first page asks who the intake is for. A couple then gets one private link per partner, and a teen's intake sends the consent pages to a parent or guardian. One branching template is one form to keep current, where three separate copies drift apart.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should an intake counseling form have?\", \"a\": \"As few as the counselor needs before the first session. Every question should change what happens in that hour or who the client sees; drop the rest. Screeners set a floor, since the PHQ-9 has nine items and the GAD-7 has seven. Time a test run on a phone and cut whatever a client would not finish in one sitting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can clients complete a counseling intake form online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. An online form goes out as a link before the first appointment, and clients fill it in on a phone and sign consent on screen. Answers arrive typed, with screener totals already added. In Emergent, each submitted form becomes a record in a database you own. Businesses outside healthcare use the same setup for a general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/intake-form'>intake form</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}